---
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title={`Privacy Policy · ${SITE.name}`}
  description="Ghostpost's Privacy Policy. How we handle your social media archives, our zero-password policy, and how we protect your personal data."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <Header />

  <main class="legal-page">
    <div class="container legal-page__inner">
      <article class="prose">
        <header class="prose__header">
          <span class="prose__badge">privacy</span>
          <h1 class="prose__title">privacy policy</h1>
          <p class="prose__date">Last updated: September 28, 2026</p>
        </header>

        <div class="prose__callout">
          <p class="prose__highlight">
            Privacy and security are the foundation of Ghostpost. We don’t sell your data. We don’t use it for advertising.
            We never touch your live social accounts. It’s your data, period.
          </p>
          <p>
            We don’t train public artificial intelligence models on your private archives. Your scan is strictly your own.
          </p>
        </div>

        <section>
          <h2>1. Our Core Privacy Commitments</h2>
          <p>Ghostpost is designed from the ground up around four foundational privacy principles:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Zero Social Passwords:</strong> We never ask for, collect, or store your social media passwords.</li>
            <li><strong>No Live Account Linking:</strong> We do not connect to your live profiles via OAuth or scrape your active feeds. You upload official data export archives that you control.</li>
            <li><strong>No Public AI Training:</strong> We never use your uploaded posts, photos, comments, or direct messages to train shared or public AI models.</li>
            <li><strong>No Data Monetization:</strong> We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal data, archives, or contact information to advertisers, data brokers, or third parties.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
          <h3>Waitlist & Contact Information</h3>
          <p>
            When you join our early-access waitlist, we collect your email address or mobile phone number, along with the source
            of your signup. We use this information solely to notify you when Ghostpost is ready for you, provide your early-access
            onboarding, and send critical transactional updates.
          </p>

          <h3>Uploaded Social Media Archives</h3>
          <p>
            To perform a scan, you voluntarily upload an official data export file (such as a .zip archive from Instagram, TikTok,
            X, Facebook, or Reddit). These archives contain your historical posts, comments, captions, dates, and media that you
            chose to export from the platform.
          </p>

          <h3>Technical Telemetry</h3>
          <p>
            We collect basic, privacy-preserving technical logs (such as IP address, browser type, and response latency) strictly
            to prevent abuse, rate-limit waitlist spam, and maintain the security and availability of our edge infrastructure.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>3. How We Process Social Archives</h2>
          <p>
            When you submit a data export zip, our automated audit engine parses the text and metadata in an isolated, ephemeral
            processing environment:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Content Categorization:</strong> Text is evaluated against reputational risk categories (such as alcohol, drugs, profanity, toxicity, or extreme hot takes).</li>
            <li><strong>Report Generation:</strong> A prioritized review dashboard is compiled for your browser session, displaying flagged items, timestamps, and direct URLs or context to help you locate them.</li>
            <li><strong>Strict Read-Only Isolation:</strong> The audit is generated exclusively for your review. Ghostpost has no ability to delete or modify posts on your live social accounts; you remain in total control of any cleanup action.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>4. Data Retention & Immediate Purge</h2>
          <p>
            We believe you should never leave data where it doesn’t belong:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>User-Initiated Purge:</strong> You can permanently purge your scan results, parsed data, and uploaded files at any time directly from your dashboard. Once confirmed, deletion from our active systems is immediate.</li>
            <li><strong>Automatic Expiration:</strong> Uploaded archive files are automatically deleted after your audit session completes or expires, unless you explicitly request temporary cloud retention for ongoing review.</li>
            <li><strong>Waitlist Removal:</strong> You can remove yourself from the waitlist at any time by clicking unsubscribe in any notification or by emailing <a href="mailto:privacy@getghostpost.com">privacy@getghostpost.com</a>.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>5. Subprocessors & Infrastructure</h2>
          <p>
            We partner with industry-leading infrastructure providers who are contractually bound by rigorous data protection
            agreements:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Cloudflare, Inc.:</strong> Edge hosting, DDoS mitigation, and serverless compute (Workers & D1 database). All traffic is encrypted in transit via TLS 1.3.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>6. Security Practices</h2>
          <p>We maintain comprehensive technical safeguards to protect your personal information:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>All connections to Ghostpost are encrypted using modern HTTPS (TLS 1.3) with HSTS enabled.</li>
            <li>Archive processing runs in isolated sandbox environments with strict access controls.</li>
            <li>We adhere to the principle of least privilege: our staff never accesses or reads your private social archives except upon your explicit request for technical support.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>7. Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            Ghostpost is intended for high school, college, and adult users preparing for higher education admissions and
            employment. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under the age of 13. If you believe a child
            under 13 has provided personal data to Ghostpost, please contact us immediately at <a href="mailto:privacy@getghostpost.com">privacy@getghostpost.com</a>, and we will promptly delete the information.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>8. California (CCPA/CPRA) & International Privacy Rights</h2>
          <p>
            Regardless of where you live, Ghostpost affords you the highest privacy standards:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Right to Know & Access:</strong> You have the right to request a copy of the personal information we hold about you.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to Delete:</strong> You have the right to request the permanent deletion of your personal data.</li>
            <li><strong>No Sale or Sharing:</strong> We do not sell your personal information and do not share it for cross-context behavioral advertising.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            To exercise any of these rights, simply email <a href="mailto:privacy@getghostpost.com">privacy@getghostpost.com</a>. We will verify and process your request within 30 days without discrimination.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>9. Security Vulnerability Disclosure</h2>
          <p>
            We welcome vulnerability reports from security researchers and developers. If you discover a vulnerability or security
            issue affecting Ghostpost, please disclose it responsibly by emailing <a href="mailto:privacy@getghostpost.com">privacy@getghostpost.com</a> with reproducible steps. We appreciate your assistance in keeping our users safe.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>10. Changes & Contact</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When changes are made, we will update the "Last updated" date
            at the top of this page and notify waitlist members of any material revisions.
          </p>
          <p>For any questions or concerns regarding our privacy practices, please contact us at:</p>
          <ul class="prose__contact-list">
            <li><strong>Privacy Officer:</strong> <a href="mailto:privacy@getghostpost.com">privacy@getghostpost.com</a></li>
            <li><strong>General Inquiries:</strong> <a href="mailto:hello@getghostpost.com">hello@getghostpost.com</a></li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    position: relative;
    padding: 144px 0 96px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 50% 0%, rgb(167 139 250 / 0.14), transparent 600px),
      var(--tint);
  }
  .legal-page__inner {
    max-width: 800px;
  }

  .prose {
    color: rgb(23 23 23 / 0.85);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .prose__header {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .prose__badge {
    display: inline-grid;
    place-items: center;
    height: 28px;
    padding: 0 12px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    color: var(--accent-deep);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .prose__title {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 5.5vw, 56px);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .prose__date {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .prose__callout {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 20px;
    padding: 24px 28px;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
    margin-bottom: 48px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .prose__highlight {
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 650;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .prose section {
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .prose h3 {
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-top: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .prose p {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .prose ul {
    margin: 16px 0 20px 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    list-style-type: disc;
  }
  .prose li {
    padding-left: 4px;
  }
  .prose a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }
  .prose a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-deep);
  }
  .prose__contact-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
    margin-left: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .legal-page { padding: 120px 0 72px; }
    .prose h2 { font-size: 20px; }
  }
</style>
